swehouse.c: SEFLG_RADIANS leaves the cusp and ascmc speeds in degrees

swe_houses_ex2() converts the positions to radians under SEFLG_RADIANS and
leaves both speed arrays in degrees per day, so a caller asking for radians is
handed the two in different units, a factor of 57.3 apart.

    #include "swephexp.h"
    #include <stdio.h>
    int main(void) {
      double cusp[13], ascmc[10], cs[13], as[10]; char serr[256];
      swe_houses_ex2(2451545.0, SEFLG_RADIANS, 52.5, 13.4, 'P',
                     cusp, ascmc, cs, as, serr);
      printf("%.9f rad, %.9f per day\n", cusp[1], cs[1]);
      return 0;
    }

      before   0.900328369 rad, 600.727650279 per day
      after    0.900328369 rad,  10.484675405 per day

swetest cannot show this one; it has no flag for radians, so the sample above is
the test.

Caller risk, and it is a large one: a caller that had compensated for
the old behaviour by dividing gets a result 57.3 times wrong, with no compile
error and no version gate to catch it. Against that, swephprg documents the
parameters as cusp_speed /* like cusps */ and ascmc_speed /* like ascmc */, and
under that flag they were not like them. Whether the correction is worth the
break is a judgement about the API, not about the arithmetic.

Positions are untouched.

This is one concern lifted out of "swehouse.c: compute house cusp speeds
analytically" so that it can be taken alone. That patch contains this change and
rewrites the surrounding code as well, so the two cannot both be applied; it is
also available as an eight-step series, of which this is one step. Independent of
every other patch in the set.

---
 swehouse.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)
diff --git a/swehouse.c b/swehouse.c
index 892c931..5172eab 100644
--- a/swehouse.c
+++ b/swehouse.c
@@ -397,6 +397,19 @@ int CALL_CONV swe_houses_ex2(double tjd_ut,
       cusp[i] *= DEGTORAD;
     for (i = 0; i < SE_NASCMC; i++)
       ascmc[i] *= DEGTORAD;
+    /* The speeds are angles per day and belong in the same unit as the angles
+     * they accompany. Without this a SEFLG_RADIANS caller was handed radian
+     * positions beside degree per day speeds, so anything that added a speed
+     * to a position, or compared the two, was out by a factor of 57.3. The
+     * omission predates this patch and mattered less while nine house systems
+     * returned interpolated speeds nobody could rely on; now that every system
+     * returns a real derivative, callers will use it. */
+    if (cusp_speed != NULL)
+      for (i = 1; i <= ito; i++)
+        cusp_speed[i] *= DEGTORAD;
+    if (ascmc_speed != NULL)
+      for (i = 0; i < SE_NASCMC; i++)
+        ascmc_speed[i] *= DEGTORAD;
   }
   if (retc_makr < 0)
     return retc_makr;
